1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,480
It‘s very common these days for people to have a gym regime.
如今，人们制定健身计划是很常见的事。

2
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:25,200
Whatever the drive behind it, whether health-related, performance-related or just plain vainglory, it is not uncommon for people to take some sort of regular exercise each week.
无论背后的驱动力是什么，是与健康相关、与运动表现相关，还是仅仅出于虚荣，人们每周进行某种定期锻炼并不罕见。

3
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,530
But if you’ve never done it before, what‘s the best way to go about it?
但如果你以前从未进行过健身，最好的方法是什么呢？

4
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:36,060
Well, many people make use of using a PT - that’s a personal trainer.
嗯，很多人会聘请PT，也就是个人健身教练。

5
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:44,200
This might be because they‘re wet behind the ears or maybe they just don’t want the aggro of designing their own workout plan.
这可能是因为他们缺乏经验，或者也许他们只是不想自己设计健身计划那么麻烦。

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:49,600
A PT will create a bespoke plan for you based on your aims.
私人教练会根据你的目标为你制定一个量身定制的计划。

7
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:58,960
They will tailor it to your current abilities and, better still, they will teach you how to move in a way that won‘t incapacitate you.
他们会根据你目前的能力进行定制，更好的是，他们会教你如何以一种不会让你受伤的方式进行运动。

8
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:06,150
However, the trade-off of getting a PT is the cost.
然而，请私人教练的弊端在于费用。

9
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:12,100
With the double whammy of paying for a PT and gym membership, the price of an hourly session can be steep.
考虑到既要支付私人教练的费用，又要支付健身房的会员费这种双重负担，每小时的课程费用可能会很昂贵。

10
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:18,890
If you‘re strapped for cash, then regular sessions might be out of your budget.
如果你手头拮据，那么定期的课程可能会超出你的预算。

11
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:20,770
So what’s left?
那么还有什么选择呢？

12
00:01:20,770 --> 00:01:24,930
Well, if you have the grit for it, you can make your own regime.
嗯，如果你有毅力，你可以制定自己的健身计划。

13
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:28,470
It‘s relatively easy to do if you have the know-how.
如果你具备专业知识，做起来会相对容易。

14
00:01:28,470 --> 00:01:32,680
But before you do, here are some basic pointers.
但在你开始之前，这里有一些基本的要点。

15
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:36,880
First, keep your fitness goal in mind.
首先，要牢记你的健身目标。

16
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:43,300
Are you looking to slim down, bulk up, get shredded or increase your abilities?
你是想减肥、增肌、练出肌肉线条还是提高你的能力呢？

17
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:49,970
Whatever it is, make sure the things you choose to do are in pursuit of that goal.
无论目标是什么，确保你选择做的事情是为了追求这个目标。

18
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:52,780
Next, do your research.
其次，做些研究。

19
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:58,160
These days, social media is chock-full of fitness videos and advice.
如今，社交媒体上充满了健身视频和建议。

20
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:10,420
Watch as many of these as possible, but make sure to be a little critical of them — everyone has a different physique and what works for one may not work for another.
尽可能多地观看这些内容，但要确保对它们保持一定的批判性——每个人的体质都不同，对一个人有效的方法可能对另一个人却并不适用。

21
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:14,230
Finally, keep your feet on the ground.
最后，要脚踏实地。

22
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:23,800
Be patient with yourself and set realistic goals — it takes at least three months to see any realistic body changes.
对自己要有耐心，设定现实的目标——至少需要三个月才能看到身体有任何明显的变化。

23
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:33,180
And don‘t be overzealous — never work in pain — a good workout is difficult and challenging, but never painful.
而且不要过于狂热——绝不要在疼痛的情况下锻炼——一次好的锻炼是困难且具有挑战性的，但绝不是痛苦的。

24
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:36,220
Pain means you are damaging yourself.
疼痛意味着你在伤害自己。

25
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:45,130
If nothing else, focus on calisthenics — these are the basic body movements which everyone can do anywhere, even at home.
如果没有别的选择，那就专注于徒手健身——这些是每个人在任何地方都能做的基本身体动作，甚至在家里也可以。

26
00:02:45,130 --> 00:02:50,780
They include squats, push-ups, pull-ups and crunches, among other things.
它们包括深蹲、俯卧撑、引体向上和仰卧起坐等等。

27
00:02:50,780 --> 00:03:02,980
Do as many of one exercise as you can without stopping, and then try and repeat that number twice more — make sure you sweat, and don‘t forget to rest for a minute in between!
尽可能多地不间断地做一种运动，然后再尝试重复同样的次数两次——确保你出汗了，而且不要忘记在中间休息一分钟！
